{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers","id":1011387,"title":"Do Animals Count As Sleepers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-02T23:17:20-08:00","id":1011387,"title":"Do Animals Count As Sleepers?","content":"Just a thought I had less than a minute before typing this.<br /> <br /> What effect does the perception of an animal have on Magick? Are animals considered Sleeper witnesses? If so, what, if anything, would be considered coincidental by a beast?<br /> <br /> I have no real ideas on the matter at this point, and don't feel much like doing what I always do: pull an Albert Einstein, and spend way more time considering a problem than is practical. What do you people think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T23:21:25-08:00","id":1011388,"title":"","content":"Think of it this way--how many of your routine actions WOULDN'T your cat think were magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T23:34:27-08:00","id":1011391,"title":"","content":"I see your point, though I have dogs not cats (like six of them; weep for me).<br /> <br /> Although that brings up another point. My dogs are always barking at the slightest sound from outside or person-shaped blob that walks past the front door windows. They may know the house and yard like the back of their paws, but as far as they know, there be dragons beyond the fence. And that's not even getting into me or the family, who do things to or around the dogs that are utterly baffling.<br /> <br /> So I would guess they have a very broad view of what's possible. Literally anything can happen, because everything is chaos, as ruled by upright-walking eldritch abominations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T23:39:33-08:00","id":1011392,"title":"","content":"No, next question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T03:09:17-08:00","id":1011438,"title":"","content":"To put it in simple, metaphysical terms:<br /> <br /> * Only beings with asleep Avatars can count as witnesses.<br /> * Only non-Mage humans have sleeping Avatars <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:09:47-08:00","id":1011546,"title":"","content":"What Ambrosia said. No Avatar, no Magick \u2014 not even to the extent of helping define or enforce the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-03-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:54:30-08:00","id":1011576,"title":"","content":"Thought Experiment:<br /> A human gets turned into a rat, and loses himself in this form (after wp days).<br /> Would this particular rat count as sleeper?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:59:31-08:00","id":1011579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011576#post1011576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thought Experiment:<br /> A human gets turned into a rat, and loses himself in this form (after wp days).<br /> Would this particular rat count as sleeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have the mind of a rat, then they no longer have the cognitive faculties required for self awareness, and awareness of the universal consensus. So probably not.<br /> <br /> If they still have the mind of a human, then they are still a sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:55:44-08:00","id":1011681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011579#post1011579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they have the mind of a rat, then they no longer have the cognitive faculties required for self awareness, and awareness of the universal consensus. So probably not.<br /> <br /> If they still have the mind of a human, then they are still a sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if the human was turned into a rat and retained their cognitive awareness, I would think they'd suddenly have a very good reason to doubt their previous understanding of reality. If they can change into a rodent, what else might be possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:47:44-08:00","id":1011703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011681#post1011681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the human was turned into a rat and retained their cognitive awareness, I would think they'd suddenly have a very good reason to doubt their previous understanding of reality. If they can change into a rodent, what else might be possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Denial is a very powerful thing.<br /> If changing into an animal was all it took to awaken a sleeper, then everyone would be doing it, especially the Verbena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:57:51-08:00","id":1011709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011703#post1011703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Denial is a very powerful thing.<br /> If changing into an animal was all it took to awaken a sleeper, then everyone would be doing it, especially the Verbena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but don't confuse suddenly having a much broader view of reality with Awakening.<br /> Sorcerers have sleeping Avatars, but they don't count as witnesses along either mystical or technological paradigms. Neither do people frequenting with nightfolk.<br /> So a sleeper's general view of 'This is the world' can change a lot - being turned into a rat might just kick the rigid structures loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:00:16-08:00","id":1011710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011703#post1011703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Denial is a very powerful thing.<br /> If changing into an animal was all it took to awaken a sleeper, then everyone would be doing it, especially the Verbena.</div> </div> </div> </div>The person doesn't need to Awaken to stop counting as a Sleeper witness. Consors and Acolytes are entirely mundane humans with nothing supernatural about them. Yet they don't count as witnesses because they've been exposed to the existence of the supernatural, and adjusted their beliefs accordingly. My argument is that a person who is turned into a rat - and retains their cognitive functions - is fully capable of realizing how unnatural this development is and, like the Consor, adjust their beliefs of what is possible accordingly.<br /> <br /> Moreover, while Denial is certainly a possible reaction to being changed into a Rat, it's by no means assured. It depends on the person and their situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:13:33-08:00","id":1011718,"title":"","content":"In fact, even Denial wouldn't necessarily keep the person as a Sleeper witness. Because even if the person were to deny the events as happening, they still need to <i>explain to themselves</i> what their senses are telling them. If they scurry around on the floor at the height of someone's foot, whipping a tail around, etc, that sort of thing can't just go ignored. It creates too much cognitive dissonance to be endured.<br /> <br /> Denial itself is a method of resolving Cognitive Dissonance, and the newly made rat has a few options. Hallucination, Dream, or Insanity are the most obvious explanations for the person's new set of sensory input, and the ones that they would likely latch onto in order to deny the reality of their situation. They don't need to invalidate their world view, because obviously their senses are wrong.<br /> <br /> But this also means that they don't trust anything they experience, and have a perfectly good reason not to. If anything, this makes them <i>more likely</i> to cease being a sleeper witness (at least as long as the duration on the transformation lasts), because they can explain everything they see. If they are hallucinating, dreaming, or stark raving mad, then it's only natural that other weird, impossible activity would go on around them. It's par for the course at that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T19:35:29-08:00","id":1011791,"title":"","content":"There is a Merit in Sorcerer Revised that allows the Sorcerer to be counted as a Sleeper for anything outside of their paradigm (Style Sleeper-2 point Merit), which I imagine that the Technocrats love in their Enlightened Citizens. There is nothing like having your enemies experience the penalties associated with vulgar magic in front of witnesses when you are effectively using coincidental magic because the witnesses accept your paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T21:08:05-08:00","id":1011829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011791#post1011791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Merit in Sorcerer Revised that allows the Sorcerer to be counted as a Sleeper for anything outside of their paradigm (Style Sleeper-2 point Merit), which I imagine that the Technocrats love in their Enlightened Citizens. There is nothing like having your enemies experience the penalties associated with vulgar magic in front of witnesses when you are effectively using coincidental magic because the witnesses accept your paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 sort of made this the default with Extraordinary Citizens. Unlike Traditionalist acolytes et al., who in a vast majority of cases grew up in modern times and so don't act as witnesses to either mystic or techno magics, Extraordinary Citizens are indoctrinated so they believe in Super Science, but not in mysticism. This goes along with the Technocracy's usual operating philosophy of keeping the true nature of Reality a secret from all but their highest ranking members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T21:14:35-08:00","id":1011832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011579#post1011579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they have the mind of a rat, then they no longer have the cognitive faculties required for self awareness</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you a psychic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T23:15:20-08:00","id":1011875,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on the nature of the magic. Ratkin rat form brains are as small as any other rat, but they maintain their sapience. I would actually rule that Animal Kinfolk are sapient enough to understand that some magick is unnatural and would react as Sleepers to any non-Gaian style of magick (Dreamspeaker and Verbena are acceptable, Order of Hermes and Sons of Ether are unacceptable). I would also rule that Human Kinfolk are likewise Sleepers for non-Gaian traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T23:26:21-08:00","id":1011878,"title":"","content":"In answer to the OP, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T00:17:31-08:00","id":1011888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011832#post1011832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you a psychic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please. We have science to prove this, thank you!<br /> <br /> I read a Q&amp;A on answers.com about this and it unequivocally stated that <a href=\"http://www.answers.com/Q/Are_rats_self_aware#slide=1\" target=\"_blank\">rats are, indeed, self aware. </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":"Today, 08:19 AM. Reason: inb4 mages become the weakest splat, since their magick gets fucky when witnessed by rats, pigeons, ect. 12-04-2016, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:43:27-08:00","id":1012112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1011888#post1011888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please. We have science to prove this, thank you!<br /> <br /> I read a Q&amp;A on answers.com about this and it unequivocally stated that <a href=\"http://www.answers.com/Q/Are_rats_self_aware#slide=1\" target=\"_blank\">rats are, indeed, self aware. </a></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Just when you thought it was safe to use vulgar magick underwater... JAWS: THE WITNESSING!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:51:05-08:00","id":1012223,"title":"","content":"Well, there is evidence that ants pass the mirror test (<a href=\"http://www.animalcognition.org/2015/04/15/list-of-animals-that-have-passed-the-mirror-test/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.animalcognition.org/2015/...e-mirror-test/</a>), so there is a question of the definition of self-awareness. It could be that there are multiple aspects of self-awareness and that some animals will pass some tests while others will fail some tests. I like to think that disbelief is an extention of empathy, the ability to disbelieve is related to the ability to project your emotions on another entity, and that animals that possess empathy are Sleepers, regardless of whether their members have passed specific tests, because they can disbelieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T18:26:50-08:00","id":1012307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1012223#post1012223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there is evidence that ants pass the mirror test (<a href=\"http://www.animalcognition.org/2015/04/15/list-of-animals-that-have-passed-the-mirror-test/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.animalcognition.org/2015/...e-mirror-test/</a>), so there is a question of the definition of self-awareness. It could be that there are multiple aspects of self-awareness and that some animals will pass some tests while others will fail some tests. I like to think that disbelief is an extention of empathy, the ability to disbelieve is related to the ability to project your emotions on another entity, and that animals that possess empathy are Sleepers, regardless of whether their members have passed specific tests, because they can disbelieve.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mirror test isn't really an exact or incredibly useful standard; it just shows that the animals in question can see light the same way that humans do. Some things are more important, like ripples in the surrounding fluid medium, or scents, or spectra of light that humans can't see (some animals are sensitive to UV, which mirrors don't reflect particularly well).<br /> <br /> Which is also interesting to consider, since other animals can detect facets of reality which unaided humans cannot, and often might not even have a clue exist, like how Chimerstry can't effectively fool werebeasts unless the vampire using it also has Auspex to enhance their senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T20:25:02-08:00","id":1012355,"title":"","content":"All good points. I think that an ST should tell players what counts as a Sleeper in their Mage games, as it can matter quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T22:11:31-08:00","id":1013595,"title":"","content":"For natural animals, there's no Avatar; so all this talk about whether or not they have self-awareness is moot. For people transformed into animals? I wouldn't worry about the sapience thing; I'd just focus on whether or not the experience has made Custos out of them. The way I figure it, it's not enough to believe in the supernatural in order to become an Extraordinary Citizen/Style Sleeper/whatever; you need to gain enough familiarity with a particular Practice to recognize a given supernatural event as something that Practice might do, and you need to believe that that particular Practice really works. Getting turned into a rat can certainly inspire the belief (though \u2014 house rule time \u2014 it can just as easily inspire Madness or Denial instead); but it does nothing in terms of the understanding. So no, I don't think that being turned into a rat makes you stop counting as a Witness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-07-2016, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:56:02-08:00","id":1013764,"title":"","content":"Here's an interesting little conundrum.<br /> <br /> If a mage believes that animal minds and beliefs are just as pivotal to shaping the consensus as humans are, and thus would agree that animals are sleepers, would magic be Vulgar with Witnesses in front of these animals?<br /> <br /> But then, what if another mage thinks that all animals are already awakened, and their magic is done in the form of Spirit work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:57:09-08:00","id":1013792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1013764#post1013764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage believes that animal minds and beliefs are just as pivotal to shaping the consensus as humans are, and thus would agree that animals are sleepers, would magic be Vulgar with Witnesses in front of these animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Pretty much for the same reason that a Mage can't make their magic coincidental by simply not believing that it is vulgar.<br /> <br /> There is one exception for both cases:<br /> The Mage's sanctum or horizon realm, as the Mage's beliefs rule reality in that place. Magick cast in front of animals would be vulgar there. Vulgar with witnesses if the Mage himself (not the animals, they still can't be witnesses!) is present for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-07-2016, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T10:29:35-08:00","id":1013828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1013792#post1013792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Pretty much for the same reason that a Mage can't make their magic coincidental by simply not believing that it is vulgar.<br /> <br /> There is one exception for both cases:<br /> The Mage's sanctum or horizon realm, as the Mage's beliefs rule reality in that place. Magick cast in front of animals would be vulgar there. Vulgar with witnesses if the Mage himself (not the animals, they still can't be witnesses!) is present for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about Reality Zones and the animals which pass through them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:25:19-08:00","id":1014003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011387-do-animals-count-as-sleepers?p=1013828#post1013828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Reality Zones and the animals which pass through them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure where you are going with that question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href