<br /> But I highly doubt even a Reality Zone can just spontaneously have Avatars conjured for every animal entering, which is still the deciding factor for 'With witnesses' or 'without witnesses'.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are all animals unawakened and therefor witnesses? Or awakened and therefor not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T06:42:22-08:00","id":1014285,"title":"","content":"Animals counting as sleepers would be a convincing reason the distant reaches of the earth default to primal reality. That said, they would have to have a much weaker impact or modern technology would be more finicky in the wilderness. You also have to get around the Avatar issue.<br /> <br /> That said, the nature of the Consensus was not always as tied into Avatars as it is in the more recent editions. I seem to recall several 2nd edition books were evasive over all Sleepers having Avatars. Mage 2nd Edition even indicated Spirits could impact the consensus, and they definitely don't have Avatars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com